{"title":"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60afefdccd9cd87ba1923010049fc21a05f99136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{N}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" /> denote the number of strictly increasing sequences of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35cac45db4dab760e45259f84e225599111ba787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\cdots, a_{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"11\" /> satisfying the following two rules<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e89270aa29dd200d6388cdaf4b31cb721b62ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$:$\" width=\"3\" height=\"7\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b02a491e6fc8db3a577b344b1a53b7a8e77e0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2046500d5c2f8b12701966eab0399e570a0def11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{19}=361,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /></li>\n<li>for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaa113bc0fc00821562a7b89fbce2a33f1f2e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\neq j,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de384159288415e68cf7b378f5de01df9d240f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{ij}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe68506dc73fa036319d8d35c7a00d0f37d12c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i \\cdot j)^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> number not in the sequence<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d198e115ee5481f6012df3f623690b4bcab5f869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"4\" height=\"5\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b069a050ed7d3071d2afa32a01e6df4ca647bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i-b_{ij})(a_j-b_{ij})&lt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Find the largest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85ca90ec0f4983dc3f221689912370a60cae2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{N}.$\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>First, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> is always increasing as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> increases. Notice that the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1f76a58bb616330fdb3082dc0f83fff39f1226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i-b_{ij})(a_j-b_{ij})&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> is equivalent to the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c2dd630fdf00358ecf961a7269f69d3a9634c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{ij}\\in(a_i,a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. The first time we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/801b4b6c57a1e85c609e277fa66555060aacd29f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca2a347abcc61267769f9dd7b7c17489ddc200c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd4020c9562e026f9cc496f7753d83bfad33faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n+1)}\\in(a_n,a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73700a25f76f0c5f1560c19f44182c5d20dc606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&lt;b_{n(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that this index of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is minimized since at all lesser indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be the smaller of the two factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d9dbe8588e6243350fc642973b9365304100da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303e32a56999639186d9d5c885c262474769133f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\ne j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />). Similarly, we note that the greatest value for which we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b951a5af0dc6ac761103e3f0bad0cf09bbc1f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a7802cbfe3287d6c3a5c8a07f40199d6189c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> since all greater indices would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> being the smaller of the two factors. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8d7f06dd839c5853f1801af0489869e6006126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n-1)}\\in(a_i,a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/78013b2d34b60460d50438aca4f6911af3e4cac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&gt;b_{n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Combining these facts, we see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb7bbe68ec8e822fadc1ed5e31570aa8fffbe6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{n(n-1)}&lt;a_n&lt;b_{n(n+1)}\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />\nand we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/0291909f635caaa6169760369e69586e4430ad51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n-1)}=n(n-1)+n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"210\" height=\"21\" /> by construction (since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d3407c16ac230a65d2dbb640f0d46dfe4e1807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> other indices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> of lesser value, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> indices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> from the inequality above). Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54fc8b562931e5fc16dfbb26692ab5fb976df3e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n(n+1)}=n(n+1)+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />. Therefore, after expanding,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a78fd4acd8677888d1c07691ceebe6ecc916aa0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2-1&lt;a_n&lt;n^2+2n\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich implies that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/959aae230d5feb14881f91e5179d8178aaadcbaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2\\le a_n\\le n^2+2n-1&lt;(n+1)^2\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />\nClearly, there are no two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the above intervals overlap (consider the squares at the extremes of this inequality) and so the location of each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> within each inequality is independent. Therefore, we consider the length of the interval; there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/19524fec4841030c49a79bffbe413d66b8e170bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+2n-1-n^2+1=2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" /> integers that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> could be in the interval. Then, if we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604fff3ce00616ee029f01c10e0fb85a2fcaa8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2,3,\\ldots,18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"17\" /> and permit them to vary, the total number of sequences is\n\\begin{align*}\nN&amp;=(2\\cdot2)(2\\cdot3)\\cdots(2\\cdot18)\\\\\n&amp;=2^{17}\\cdot18!\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nWe can calculate that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980652235199d55d04b7f9da22c5ac8cb491234c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6206a741f6f1c340dd442571e3df80856d913f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+4+2+1=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60cecab1ff6cf50eca3f78699b38fd5b4d30175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16+17=\\boxed{033}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I (page does not exist)\">2019 CIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 CIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173453\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 323/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1788/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 110/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8874/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   53.461      1 -total\n 90.22%   48.235      1 Template:CIME_box\n  9.37%    5.009      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19844:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173453 and revision id 246821. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}